<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tony Blair</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tony Blair is a British Labour politician who was prime minister of the United Kingdom from 1997 to 2007, the party's longest-serving holder of the office. Leading New Labour to three election victories, he introduced devolution for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, helped secure the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/good-friday-agreement">Good Friday Agreement</a> in Northern Ireland, and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> into the wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tony-blair.jpg" alt="Tony Blair" width="320" height="493" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pavel Golovkin · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tony_Blair_(2010).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 1990s many parties adopted the Third Way, an attempt to combine social democratic values with economic liberalism, embraced most notably by Bill Clinton’s New Democrats and <b>Tony Blair</b>’s New Labour; some analysts call it neoliberal.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/social-democracy">Social democracy · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>Under <b>Tony Blair</b> the leadership was said to play it down; Jeremy Corbyn's supporters sang it when he was elected leader in 2015.</blockquote><a href="/songs/the-red-flag">The Red Flag</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=55.95,-3.19&amp;year=1988" aria-label="Edinburgh on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4481 258 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Tony Blair"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4931 528h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4931 528h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=55.95,-3.19&amp;year=1988">What was here in 1988? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
